finding: P1: The new atlas slot binding crashes a supported composition when the shadow-fitting main camera is a depth-only attachView registration and another camera presents. ShadowCameraSystem picks the first Camera+StandardRenderer regardless of presentation; BeginFrameSystem assigns the main depth-only View.slot = shadeCount, but allocates/uploads ViewUniforms only for presenting slots. shadowViewSlot now passes that depth-only cull slot to engineGroup, whose RenderContext.viewBuffers[slot] is undefined. Independently reproduced at d74a7721 in a git-archive scratch tree by changing the sprite shadow fixture's initial main attachTexture to attachView and adding one Camera+StandardRenderer sibling with a 32x32 attachTexture: first world.step throws System StandardRendering/shadowmap: 'view' is a resource required to populate bind group layout engineLayout, at renderCascades atlas.ts:1100 -> engineGroup pipelines.ts:331. The identical fixture and clip-shadow test passes at 69e2fd07. Previously allocated buffers can mask the crash but then bind stale unrelated camera uniforms. A View.slot is not necessarily an uploaded shading slot; the fix needs to handle a fitting camera with no presenting ViewUniforms rather than treating its cull slot as one. The submitted swap test does correctly fail at base with 970/65536 differing texels and pass at HEAD, but both cameras in that witness present, so it misses this regression.
